# Supply-chain guard (Semgrep npm-missing-minimum-release-age, 2026-09-18).
# npm builds the dependency tree from versions that have been published for at
# least this many days, so a freshly published malicious version is not pulled
# in by the next `npm install` / `npm update`. Documented behaviour (npm 12
# `npm help config`): if no version of a dependency satisfies the window the
# command errors; `npm audit fix` warns and exits non-zero when the patch is
# too new. To take a same-day release on purpose, either run once with
# `--min-release-age=0` or list the package under `min-release-age-exclude`.
min-release-age=7
